# Ushant to Falmouth (ushant-to-falmouth), the scripted captain (in the game, at the captain's station); seed 7; 907 lines, the digest b681a27dc0db7a0d
* Morning watch, 8 bells (04:00)  The passage for gate 5b, Ushant to Falmouth. Wind SW, 15 knots, a moderate breeze. Heading N (357°).
* Morning watch, 8 bells (04:00)  The land about Keller on the larboard quarter, bearing SW by S, distant a mile.
* Morning watch, 8 bells (04:00)  Keller bearing SW, distant three miles.
* Morning watch, 8 bells (04:00)  Ushant bearing SW, distant three miles.
* Morning watch, 8 bells (04:00)  Molène bearing SSE, distant two leagues.
* Morning watch, 8 bells (04:00)  Béniguet bearing SSE, distant two leagues.
* Morning watch, 8 bells (04:00)  The light on Ushant bearing SW by S, distant two miles.
  Morning watch, 8 bells (04:00)  Order: set plain sail.
  Morning watch, 8 bells (04:00)  The captain takes the station (the scripted captain, through the game); sampled every glass and on notable and urgent events, in lockstep.
* Morning watch, 8 bells (04:00)  The captain's station has the deck (Captain Bowen); the ship is commanded from it, by direct orders and by the book.
  Morning watch, 8 bells (04:00)  By the captain: shaping a course for falmouth outer road via 50 00 n 4 57 w.
  Morning watch, 8 bells (04:00)  Shaped a course for 50 00 n 4 57 w: N by account, 90 miles. She has no way on to work an allowance by: the flood, a quarter of a knot to the NE is not allowed for in the course; shape it again when she has gathered way; then Falmouth outer road. Helm ordered: steer N (2°).
  Morning watch, 8 bells (04:00)  Order not carried out ('trim sails'): There is no wind to trim to.
  Morning watch, 8 bells (04:00)  [captain] The captain stands by until a glass; the standing orders hold the deck.
